 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Anesthesia Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an anesthesia consent form?\", \"a\": \"An anesthesia consent form is the patient's signed agreement to a specific anesthetic plan, such as general anesthesia or monitored anesthesia care. It names who will give the anesthetic and records that the risks and alternatives were explained. ANZCA expects it to carry a signature of its own, apart from the consent for the operation.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an anesthesia consent form?\", \"a\": \"Write down the anesthetic plans and the pre-op questions first, starting from the wording your hospital already uses. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> builds the form from that wording, along with the check-in screen and a list of every signed copy.\"}, {\"q\": \"How long is an anesthesia consent form good for?\", \"a\": \"Your facility's policy sets the limit, and the form should record the date and the case it covers. In hospitals, CMS requires a pre-anesthesia evaluation within 48 hours before surgery. Signing the consent at that visit keeps the two dates close, and a case that moves gets both again. Emergent can build the form to store each signed consent with its date in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I turn a paper anesthesia consent form template into an online form?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Paste the template's wording, or the text of an anesthesia consent form PDF, into Emergent and it builds the form, with a risk section for each plan and a signature step. Keep the layout your providers already know. A general <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/consent'>consent form</a> works the same way for other agreements.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should a patient sign the anesthesia consent form?\", \"a\": \"Before any sedative premedication. Consent needs capacity, and medicine that alters mental status can take it away. ANZCA warns against asking a patient to sign after sedative premedication has been given. Schedule the anesthesia signature at the pre-op visit, never in the procedure room.\"}, {\"q\": \"What makes an anesthesia consent form valid?\", \"a\": \"Capacity, disclosure, and voluntariness, and the form can show each one. A risk section written for the chosen plan covers disclosure, a signature taken before any sedative protects capacity, and a line saying the patient may decline speaks to voluntariness. ANZCA adds that a signature without the conversation is not consent.\"}, {\"q\": \"Who signs an anesthesia consent form as the provider?\", \"a\": \"The anesthesia provider, not the surgeon. AANA lists obtaining informed consent for anesthesia among a CRNA's duties before a procedure. When an anesthesiologist supervises, your group's policy says which of the two signs as the provider.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can one anesthesia consent form also cover the operation?\", \"a\": \"It can share a page, but anesthesia still needs a signature of its own. ANZCA accepts a single form when anesthesia has a separate signature or acknowledgment. Hospital Conditions of Participation also require a properly executed consent in the chart before surgery, except in emergencies. A surgery consent form covers the operation itself.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does an anesthesia consent form record express or implied consent?\", \"a\": \"Express consent. Consent can be given in words or in writing, or implied by actions, and a signed anesthesia consent form puts it in writing. The patient signs after hearing the risks and the other options, which makes it informed consent too.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an anesthesia consent form ask pre-anesthesia questions?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Add a fasting time and a question about family history of problems with anesthesia. Malignant hyperthermia, for example, is an inherited disorder triggered by volatile anesthetic gases and succinylcholine. Ask Emergent for a rule that flags an answer like that for the anesthesiologist before the day of the case.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
